  "configuration_id": "config_014",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (best: scVI/multi/avgpool at 0.650), while the sole image test (ResNet50, single-profile) yielded only 0.208 accuracy, suggesting the image modality may carry little signal. However, ResNet50 is a relatively weak encoder; ViT-L (ImageNet-pretrained) is substantially more expressive and could extract features that ResNet50 missed. Uncertainty: We cannot yet determine whether the image modality is fundamentally uninformative for this task or simply poorly encoded. This experiment (config_014: image_only, multiprofile, ViT-L, avgpool) isolates the image encoder quality question while holding profile setting and aggregation at their known-best values (multiprofile + avgpool), avoiding confounds. If ViT-L still yields very low accuracy, we can confidently rule out the image modality and focus remaining budget on RNA-only optimization or fusion strategy. If it yields a meaningful signal, it justifies investing in multimodal experiments. This is the highest-information experiment available because it resolves a binary design question (is image useful at all?) that gates an entire family of ~36 multimodal configurations."
}

